  usilic - Text Console Buffer
  version 1.5b-1  20 Mar 2000
  Coded by Taketo Matsubara

  11..  IInnttrroodduuccttiioonn

  _U_s_i_l_i_c is a file viewer that works on a text-terminal.  It can be used on
  LLiinnuuxx or FFrreeeeBBSSDD

  22..  EEnnvviirroonnmmeenntt

  _U_s_i_l_i_c has been compiled and run on the following environments:

     LLiinnuuxx

           Debian GNU/Linux 2.1
           RedHat Linux v6.0

     FFrreeeeBBSSDD

           4.0-RELEASE

  33..  IInnssttaallllaattiioonn

  Edit _c_o_n_f_i_g_._s_h accordingly and then type `mmaakkee iinnssttaallll' as a super
  user.

  44..  손손서서

  I make my acknowledgement with thanks to following persons who sent me
  bug reports and suggestions while I have developed _u_s_i_l_i_c.

  Tomio Narita <narita@mt.cs.keio.ac.jp> agreed to add _l_v to _u_s_i_l_i_c's
  program list.  (Multilingual file viewer _l_v can be get from the WWW
  page `LV Homepage' hhttttpp::////wwwwww..mmtt..ccss..kkeeiioo..aacc..jjpp//ppeerrssoonn//nnaarriittaa//llvv//)

  Emiko Hall <emhall@ilap.com> pointed out the bug that _u_s_i_l_i_c's Japanese
  manual page can't be displayed on the default environment and reported
  other faults about usage.

  Harumichi Takahashi <hal@terry.nagaokaut.ac.jp> reported the problem
  caused by the fault of description about _k_o_n on FFrreeeeBBSSDD.

  Kazuhiko Kiriyama <kiri@kiri.toba-cmt.ac.jp> pointed out the
  difficulty of key-assignments.  He tested ppoorrtt and gave me advice
  about it.

  Pierstorff <arne.p@t-online.de> suggested to support function about
  refering to a RRPPMM package and a huge archive file, and pointed out
  incorrect code that fails to compilation.

